! ======================================================================
! test_v110_h2o_pbe_rt_stationary -- RT-TDDFT ladder step 1:
! field-free propagation of the converged ground state must be
! STATIONARY (the "do-nothing" test).
!
! Water PBE/STO-3G, C1, gas phase; 100 exponential-midpoint steps of
! dt = 0.2 au (4.8 fs is not needed for this test -- 20 au suffice to
! expose any drift).
!
! Reference (v1.10.0, 1 thread, reference BLAS):
!   Reference SCF energy:        -75.227762250396
!   RT self-check |E(0)-E_scf|:   ~2e-13  (hard-gated below 1e-6)
!   Conservation summary over 100 steps:
!     max |E(t) - E(0)|   ~ 7e-13 Ha
!     max |N_e(t) - N_e|  ~ 9e-14 e
!     max idempotency     ~ 2e-14
!     max |mu(t) - mu(0)| ~ 2e-11 au
!   All four sit at the SCF-convergence / round-off floor; the dipole
!   drift is the [F,P] residual of the converged SCF (tightening
!   %scf_ptol shrinks it further -- demonstrated in
!   BENCHMARK_NOTES_v1.10.0.md).
!   The predictor-corrector reports 1.000 iterations/step (a
!   stationary density converges the midpoint Fock immediately).
! ======================================================================
%method  PBE
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%rt_tddft 100
%rt_dt    0.2
%rt_print_every 20
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
